From 595021ba139e9ff834374603cfae1f040e2efb7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:19:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix table cell detection, save errors, handwriting
 regions

Table OCR
- New table_structure.py builds the grid from the page image: ruling
  lines first, then the table model, then the text lines, per axis.
  Deskews the region (quad angle + projection refine) and maps cell
  quads back, so rotated scans keep straight rows.
- Spans from missing rules (colspan/rowspan), header rows from <th> or
  first-row spans; ruling_style detected.
- Each OCR line goes to one cell; a line spanning a whole row is split
  by where the ink is, not copied into every cell.
- Removed the 2x2 placeholder grids (mock/paddle) that replaced real
  structure; adapters get the deskewed crop; TATR returns raw row/col
  boxes; empty cells with ink are read with the recognizer.

Saving
- PUT /annotation takes raw JSON so _clean_payload runs before
  validation (a .5 bbox or leftover key no longer 422s).
- Line key order: handwritten after table_index/cell_id (matches the
  reference pages; saved JSON is now byte-identical to the sample).
- Editor: one saveCurrent() for Save, Ctrl/Cmd+S and Submit; shows
  Saving/Saved/errors, asks before overwriting on 409, keeps edits made
  during the request marked unsaved.

Handwriting
- New handwriting boxes get subtype "note" + handwritten true; subtype
  picker; export marks their lines handwritten.

Tests: backend/tests/test_table_structure.py (10 cases).

